WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
01 · OVERVIEW: Decode how media messages shape your reaction. Photos, clips & memes persuade faster than text—slow down and inspect them.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
02 · FIVE QUESTIONS: Who created this, why, and what was left out?. Every crop, music track, and headline frames a chosen angle or emotion.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
03 · RECYCLED CLIPS: Check original date, weather, and location cues. Old disaster clips or movie scenes are frequently reposted as breaking news.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
04 · SPONSORED ADS: Spot #ad, paid partnerships & sensational clickbait. Outrage headlines maximize ad impressions rather than balanced clarity.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
05 · SYNTHETIC CUES: Watch for cuts, mismatched shadows & AI artifacts. Verify surprising speeches against official unedited full broadcasts.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
06 · TRY IT: Reverse-check one viral image or clip before sharing. Sharing unverified outrage harms real people; confirm full context first.
